{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790538523,"nonce":"+zzC3YSJS5zdPxa4dJZDkS5D/AE=","message":"The embedded wasm build (wlift.js, the playground) does not have these modules either. src/runtime/core/mod.rs compiles crypto, fs, hash, http, isolate, os, proc, socket, thread and zip only with the host feature, so an import there ends with \"Could not load module\", and each hatch package's README says Native only, pointing wasm builds at @hatch:web (fetch, WebSocket, SubtleCrypto), @hatch:assets and storage instead. So the fix is to match that build, not to port anything: the same \"Could not load module\" error at startup, and at build time for a wasm target. The browser bridges behind those alternatives (wasm/src/browser.rs, dom.rs, storage.rs) are the one part a wasm AOT program in a browser could reuse. Their Rust side is foreign methods registered as plugin symbols; only the JS imports go through wasm_bindgen shims on globalThis, which wlift.js already implements.","files":null}]}